    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That math works out to the daily maximum (3,000–4,000mg depending on guidance), but a few cautions: taking the max dose repeatedly, especially if you're dehydrated, skipping meals, or have had any alcohol, lowers your safety margin considerably. Also, acetaminophen doesn't work better at higher doses for some people, and if 1,000mg every 6 hours isn't touching it, more of the same drug often won't either.\n\nFor sleep tonight specifically, an option many people use is pairing acetaminophen with an NSAID like ibuprofen (e.g., Advil) — they work differently and can be taken together safely **if** you have no kidney issues, stomach ulcers, or blood thinner use. That often handles pain better than maxing out Tylenol alone. Still, given how miserable you feel and that these are repeated max doses, a quick call to a pharmacist or doctor is genuinely worth it.",
